{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1559503-orbit-soul-proxemics-shenanigans","id":1559503,"title":"Orbit Soul Proxemics Shenanigans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-18T08:22:39-07:00","id":1559503,"title":"Orbit Soul Proxemics Shenanigans","content":"I've been reading this charm from the Infernal manuscript, and it seems like an incredibly powerful Charm once the Key is purchased; even for Essence 3. What (if anything) am I misreading here? The base Charm allows:<ul><li>Touch-based Perception rolls at range, through barriers (penalty based on thickness) - default short, but eventually long range w/the Mind-Hand Manipulation and this Charm's Key. Subjects of her &quot;active attention&quot; have to make their own Perception roll to even know she's actively touching them</li> <li>A two-dice bonus on said touch-based Awareness rolls, <i>including those which oppose Stealth</i></li> <li>Ignores two points of penalty for examining small details</li> <li>Upon purchase of the Key, can &quot;instantly scan and visualize objects and tangible phenomena like wind within range <i>without a roll</i>&quot; to learn spatial details</li> </ul>So I have a vague idea of what a touch-based Perception roll would be.. but I don't understand how it's applicable to Stealthed opponents? If I'm showing &quot;active attention&quot; via touch to someone in Stealth, don't I have to already know where they are? Otherwise how am I touching them?<br /> <br /> It seems like this Charm is meant to work similarly to the Lunar's echolocation via Echo-Drinking Awareness, turning the Infernal into a psychic touch-based Daredevil. But the Key upgrade removes the need to even make a roll to detect anything - instead giving instant spatial details on anything you can touch. How does that not defeat any sort of Stealth that hasn't actively removed a person's physical presence from the world? Is the Charm really meant to allow an Infernal to effectively stand outside a building, and automatically know - via touch - the shape and location of every person standing inside it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26550-adayinverse","name":"adayinverse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T07:15:56-07:00","id":1559522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adayinverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1559503-orbit-soul-proxemics-shenanigans#post1559503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a vague idea of what a touch-based Perception roll would be.. but I don't understand how it's applicable to Stealthed opponents? If I'm showing &quot;active attention&quot; via touch to someone in Stealth, don't I have to already know where they are? Otherwise how am I touching them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You might know or suspect somebody is present but hiding without knowing the specifics, or just generally on alert in a manner that amounts to flailing your hands around hoping to catch something. <br /> <br /> Think of it like trying to navigate through a room that might have walls or furniture in the dark; you have your hands held out in front of you so that if anything is in the way, you'll feel it that way before you collide with it.<br /> <br /> I would interpret a difference there concerning &quot;active attention&quot; in which people have a chance to feel invisible hands upon them if the Exalt is scrutinising them specifically and deliberately, but not if they're just generally on alert to brush up against things (which should really only convey information of &quot;a thing is there&quot; by default).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adayinverse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like this Charm is meant to work similarly to the Lunar's echolocation via Echo-Drinking Awareness, turning the Infernal into a psychic touch-based Daredevil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or like Countless Grasping Phantoms for Abyssals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adayinverse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Key upgrade removes the need to even make a roll to detect anything - instead giving instant spatial details on anything you can touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the information provided by the Key is a little less good than what you would get from sight by just looking at a thing under normal circumstances. Rolls would still be needed like how you would roll Awareness to observe something more closely to discern finer or more subtle details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adayinverse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that not defeat any sort of Stealth that hasn't actively removed a person's physical presence from the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>I gather that the Charm still requires a sense of directed attention, rather than just being surrounded by a field of perfect awareness. I would say that a Stealth roll should convey a person moving in a manner that generally makes it harder to know that they're there. whether that be continuously being somewhere their opponent is not currently scrutinising, or carrying themselves in a manner that obscures being a person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adayinverse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Charm really meant to allow an Infernal to effectively stand outside a building, and automatically know - via touch - the shape and location of every person standing inside it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps over a few turns of running their invisible hands over everything (possibly creating repeated opportunities for people to notice).<br /> <br /> Otherwise it goes back to &quot;this conveys slightly less information than sight&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T11:45:04-07:00","id":1559527,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much! That makes things more clear, especially with the context from that Abyssal charm. I wasn't aware of that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26550-adayinverse","name":"adayinverse","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}